                <pb facs="0820" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6351 U.S. Steel Corporation/20:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Walton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-22T18:00:00-04:00">August 22, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Your 55, July 26, noon.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Please keep the Department closely informed by telegraph of any
                        developments that may follow the Liberian Government’s discontinuance of
                        negotiations with Neep, particularly should any conflict arise which might
                        affect adversely the proposed operations of the United States Steel
                        Corporation.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>For your confidential information, the Steel Corporation has been
                        requested by the Amsterdamsche Bank to receive a delegation which Neep
                        proposes to send to the United States with a view to inviting American
                        participation in its “initialed” iron ore concession in Liberia. The
                        Department understands that this proposal is not meeting with a favorable
                        reception by the Corporation.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
